  "reason": "Evidence: The best result so far is config_002 (rna_only, multiprofile, pca_n2000, avgpool) at 0.591 acc, showing that multiprofile + avgpool aggregation is the strongest RNA-only configuration, and PCA serves as a simple baseline encoder. Image-only is very weak (0.208), so RNA representation quality is the primary lever. Question: Does replacing PCA with a learned scVI encoder (scvi_n200) improve accuracy in the already-validated best profile/aggregation setting? This is a clean single-variable change from config_002, isolating the RNA encoder effect. Why this experiment: With 5 experiments remaining, establishing whether a learned encoder beats PCA in the best setting is critical for deciding whether to invest further budget in RNA encoder variants (scgpt) or pivot to multimodal fusion. If scvi_n200 helps, we have a clear exploitation path; if not, we confirm PCA suffices and can focus remaining budget on multimodal configurations."
}

